        "note": "The Lean development accompanying the companion paper \"Even integral parts of powers of quadratic Pisot numbers\" (repository directory Even-Integral), which classifies 𝒮 versus 𝒵 for the quadratic Pisot numbers. Same author, same collaboration, same namespace SZ, and two modules shared byte for byte: SZ/Defs.lean (the sets 𝒵 and 𝒮, tail closure, the perfect-square cell) and SZ/Tijdeman.lean (the even greedy giving [3,∞) ⊆ 𝒵, which is the m ≥ 9 cell here and one of five cells there). Beyond that common base the two developments are disjoint: neither one's theorems are used by the other, the classes they treat do not overlap (√m is neither Pisot nor Salem), and the methods differ — trace recurrences there, restricted-digit Cantor arithmetic here.",
